        DISPOSITION BA GAP CLOSURE - TRANCHE 3 ONLY (Approvals).
        Built 2026-08-31 for agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t3-design.md.

        WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. manifest/package.xml is the FULL-ORG RETRIEVE manifest and a
        source-dir deploy of force-app has the same problem: either would sweep several OTHER
        concurrent streams' undeployed, unreviewed work into usman-dpeg. Nothing below is
        wildcarded; a wildcard re-introduces the sweep.

        DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED, though modified in the tree:
        - flexipages/Opportunity_Record_Page - belongs to a concurrent stream, NOT Tranche 3.
        - Every Tranche 1 and Tranche 2 component. Both are already live
          (0Afiw000000UCLVCA4 at 14:18 UTC, 0Afiw000000UJwTCAW at 16:55 UTC on 2026-08-31);
          re-shipping them widens this deploy's blast radius for no gain.
        - quickActions/NDA__c.Move_to_Approved - DELETED from disk in this tranche. A deletion
          is not expressible here; it is PREPARED, NOT AUTHORISED in
          manifest/disposition-t3-destructive/ and needs explicit sign-off. The bypass it
          represented is already closed by other means (its FlexiPage placement is removed and
          RecordStageAdvanceService no longer maps 'Prepare'), so this is drift hygiene, not a
          live hole.

        DEPLOY ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING AND ONE CONSTRAINT IS NEW THIS TRANCHE.
        DPEG_Apex_Access now names DispositionApprovalTrackerController, which is NOT yet in the
        org. A classAccesses entry naming a missing class fails the deploy of the WHOLE
        permission set, taking all 75 grants with it. The permission set must therefore land in
        the SAME payload as the Apex or LATER - never earlier. One package satisfies that.
        The mirror hazard is worse and silent: shipping the Apex WITHOUT the grant deploys green
        and renders the new tracker "unavailable" on every Disposition record page for every
        principal and analyst, while an admin smoke test passes (Modify All Data bypasses class
        access). Both halves ship together or neither does.

        PERMISSION SETS REPLACE, THEY DO NOT MERGE - AND ONE OF THESE IS THE ADMIN-ADJACENT SET.
        All three below were reconciled against the live org by SOQL across FieldPermissions +
        ObjectPermissions + SetupEntityAccess. DPEG_Apex_Access measured 74/74 classAccesses with
        zero org-only grants and carries no field or object permissions at all. Re-run the
        three-way reconciliation immediately before deploying: other streams are active in this
        working tree and the org has taken two deploys today.

        WHAT A DEPLOY CANNOT PROVE HERE. The org holds ZERO Disposition__c records, so neither
        headline AC is discharged by shipping this: "three assignees appear on the approval
        request" and "the override reason renders on the approval page" are browser facts on a
        seeded sale. NDA_Issue_Approval is AdminOnly, so a submitted NDA LOCKS - the Recall route
        added to NDA_Record_Page and the NDA layout in this same wave is unverified until a real
        record exists. Do not report those ACs as met on a green deploy.
    -->

